fix(bundled-dev): reject requests to HMR patch files in non potentially trustworthy origins

To avoid HMR patch files (that is used for full bundle mode) to be fetched from untrusted origins (like the other requests), there was a middleware to block those requests by checking `Sec-Fetch-*` headers. This did not work for non-[potentially trustworthy origins](https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-secure-contexts/#is-origin-trustworthy) because browsers doesn't send the headers for them.

This PR replaces that by ensuring an ESM syntax to exist in HMR patch files.

close #21849 (indirectly)

